WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.042 --> 00:00:01.501
♪♪

00:00:01.501 --> 00:00:05.380
Justin Paul:
Making a musical, it’s so
special and it's so thrilling

00:00:06.381 --> 00:00:07.966
Justin Paul:
because for one brief moment,

00:00:08.634 --> 00:00:10.802
Justin Paul:
you're watching hundreds of
people 

00:00:10.802 --> 00:00:13.222
all speak the same language at
the same time.

00:00:13.263 --> 00:00:17.267
♪♪

00:00:17.601 --> 00:00:20.020
Ian Eisendrath:
This is one fifty-five for one
fifty-seven.

00:00:20.395 --> 00:00:24.024
Ian Eisendrath:
We want to make sure it’s sort
of forte piano and massive crescendo. 

00:00:24.524 --> 00:00:25.192
Ian Eisendrath:
Okay.

00:00:25.901 --> 00:00:30.822
♪♪

00:00:31.531 --> 00:00:34.534
♪♪

00:00:34.534 --> 00:00:35.994
Ian Eisendrath:
The musical brief for Spirited

00:00:35.994 --> 00:00:39.623
is to create a score that
becomes a Christmas classic.

00:00:40.457 --> 00:00:43.252
Justin Paul:
So much of our process is
strategizing, 

00:00:43.252 --> 00:00:46.129
“How does this song deliver what
we need to deliver for each
moment?”

00:00:46.505 --> 00:00:53.512
♪Am I forever unredeemable?♪

00:00:54.930 --> 00:00:57.015
Benj Pasek:
When you’re working on a script
you kind of, it’s like a flashlight

00:00:57.015 --> 00:00:59.226
where you can only see a little
bit in front of you and then you
have to have faith 

00:00:59.226 --> 00:01:00.227
Benj Pasek:
that you can keep going.

00:01:00.519 --> 00:01:02.396
Benj Pasek:
And like, things reveal
themselves to you the more you

00:01:02.396 --> 00:01:05.732
sort of shine that light and
eventually you get to where
you’re going.

00:01:05.774 --> 00:01:07.943
Ensemble singing:
♪We have to believe inside♪

00:01:07.943 --> 00:01:09.820
Ensemble singing:
♪the worst of us♪

00:01:09.820 --> 00:01:12.322
Ensemble singing:
♪there is some decency there.♪

00:01:12.322 --> 00:01:15.575
Mark Sonnenblick:
Sometimes you find an incredible
moment of emotion

00:01:15.575 --> 00:01:17.744
Mark Sonnenblick:
for a character or an idea that
could become

00:01:17.744 --> 00:01:22.249
musicalized that just leaps out
of the dialogue and becomes a
song.

00:01:22.249 --> 00:01:25.961
♪I am forever unredeemable!♪

00:01:25.961 --> 00:01:28.171
Ensemble:
♪Unredeemable!♪

00:01:28.171 --> 00:01:30.882
Justin Paul:
The great thing about this story
is it goes to so

00:01:30.882 --> 00:01:33.051
Justin Paul:
many different places because
the material

00:01:33.051 --> 00:01:35.429
and the plot allowed us to just
go there each time.

00:01:35.470 --> 00:01:37.097
Clint:
♪Oh it would be sure,

00:01:37.431 --> 00:01:38.265
simple.♪

00:01:38.557 --> 00:01:42.978
It has everything from a epic,
Bernard Herrmann film score-

00:01:43.020 --> 00:01:44.938
Ensemble singing:
♪We're bringing back
Christmas!♪

00:01:44.938 --> 00:01:47.607
Clint:
♪And all the joy that we’ve
lost!♪

00:01:47.733 --> 00:01:49.901
To contemporary pop gospel.

00:01:50.193 --> 00:01:53.155
♪That’s the view from here.♪

00:01:53.155 --> 00:01:56.742
To a big, London British
musical.

00:01:56.825 --> 00:02:00.120
Clint/Present/Ensemble:
♪I was walking through the
streets of London-town♪

00:02:00.495 --> 00:02:03.957
Clint/Present/Ensemble:
♪where freaky sleep will wake me
up and strip your people down!♪

00:02:04.708 --> 00:02:07.794
Sukari Jones:
It was so fun to contain all
these different

00:02:07.794 --> 00:02:10.130
facets and then mesh them
together.

00:02:11.173 --> 00:02:13.300
We had a ton of opportunities to
bring in

00:02:13.300 --> 00:02:15.010
dancers and big choirs and,

00:02:15.010 --> 00:02:18.388
which is just a thrill to get to
record them and, and have that
sound.

00:02:18.430 --> 00:02:21.641
Ensemble:
♪You're gonna wanna say♪

00:02:21.641 --> 00:02:24.269
Khiyon Hursey:
This score has been
mind-blowing.

00:02:24.353 --> 00:02:27.564
I’ve never heard anything like
this in my entire life.

00:02:27.689 --> 00:02:28.899
Ensemble:
♪So do a little good!♪

00:02:28.899 --> 00:02:30.400
Clint/Present:
♪Do a little good!♪

00:02:30.400 --> 00:02:30.859
Ensemble:
♪Give a little more!♪

00:02:30.859 --> 00:02:32.819
Justin Paul:
It’s a very special experience.

00:02:33.028 --> 00:02:35.697
Justin Paul:
I don’t know that we’ll ever get
this kind of chance, or this kind of

00:02:35.697 --> 00:02:38.492
experience again so we’re trying
to soak up every single minute
of it.

00:02:38.617 --> 00:02:45.082
Ensemble:
♪Do a little good!♪

